", \"12-08\", \"​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​\", \"12-30\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"01-22\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"02-12\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"03-08\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"03-30\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"04-20\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"05-11\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\", \"​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\"]\n    y-axis \"Nasdaq Composite\"\n    line [24562, 24686, 24847, 25206, 24968, 25341, 25495, 25465, 25462, 25775, 25699, 26021, 25882, 25948, 26033, 25507, 26017, 25487, 25345, 26002, 25567, 25885, 26038, 26509, 26324, 26543, 26554, 25850, 26468, 26641, 26319, 25911, 25690, 25580, 25688, 25040, 25638, 25741, 26059, 26208, 26466, 26709, 26650]\n    line [24562, 24400, 24529, 24751, 24662, 24687, 24682, 24908, 24731, 24828, 25039, 24626, 24711, 25014, 25246, 25123, 24595, 24065, 23089, 23066, 23413, 23613, 23314, 23647, 24007, 24110, 24156, 24339, 24613, 24765, 24615, 24202, 24007, 23480, 23716, 23188, 23724, 23806, 24426, 24744, 24125, 23869, 23586]\n    line [24562, 24818, 25180, 25487, 25594, 25851, 25923, 25993, 26375, 26421, 26771, 27336, 27634, 27753, 26871, 27580, 26451, 26343, 27477, 26936, 27384, 27094, 27712, 27536, 28104, 28494, 27860, 27985, 27787, 27522, 27294, 27491, 27666, 28133, 28221, 28664, 27900, 28135, 28420, 28343, 28231, 28278, 28347]\n    line [24562, 25365, 25588, 26389, 27167, 27725, 27576, 27985, 28726, 29575, 29851, 29842, 30546, 29302, 30449, 31597, 32481, 32666, 34575, 35524, 33919, 35985, 35297, 36906, 36699, 35361, 34406, 34471, 34020, 34851, 34193, 34158, 35649, 35479, 36186, 35694, 36273, 36950, 38139, 38337, 38488, 37006, 37081]\n    line [27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600, 27600]\n```\n\nSeries: 🟦 Analog median, 🟥 Analog 25th percentile, 🟩 Analog 75th percentile, 🟧 Best match: Nasdaq after 19 Oct 1998, 🟪 6 Oct 2026 closing high (27,600). Source: https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/%5EIXIC/history\n\nIn the table, \"4–7% pullback\" means every past case where the index was 4–7% below a high set 3–9 weeks earlier, as it is now. \"All periods\" means any day in history.\n\n| | S&P: 10 matches | S&P: 4–7% pullback (73 cases) | S&P: all periods | Nasdaq: 10 matches | Nasdaq: 4–7% pullback (41 cases) | Nasdaq: all periods |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Median return, 3 months | −2.6% | +4.8% | +2.7% | +5.4% | +3.6% | +3.6% |\n| Median return, 6 months | −3.1% | +6.5% | +5.2% | +8.5% | +10.5% | +7.0% |\n| Share higher after 6 months | 40% | 75% | 71% | 60% | 76% | 70% |\n| Median worst drop within 6 months | −7.4% | −2.9% | | −4.1% | −7.3% | |\n\n**What I'd take from it:**\n\n1. **Even a full replay of 2000 is mild in the near term.** After the S&P's best match (4 May 2000), the index was **+3.0% three months later and +0.8% after six**. Its worst point in that time was −5.7%. In 2000 the real damage came 6–30 months later, so the analog points to a choppy top, not an immediate collapse.\n2. **The S&P matches lean flat to lower, and the risk is in the tails.** 3 of the 10 fell more than 17% within six months: 1966, Dec 2019 (into the Covid crash) and Oct 1987. On the other side, ordinary 4–7% pullbacks recovered about 75% of the time.\n3. **The two indices point to different years.** The Nasdaq's best match is **October 1998**, which was followed by +51% in six months during the final blow-off. The S&P's best match is just *after* the 2000 top. In 1998–2000 the two moved together, so both analogs can't play out. That conflict is the clearest sign not to lean on any single match.\n4. **Rough ranges for the next six months** (middle half of the matches, 25th to 75th percentile):\n   - **S&P: about 6,850–7,500.** The median, about 7,200, stays below the high.\n   - **Nasdaq: about 23,600–28,300.** The median is about 26,650.\n5. **Levels to watch:**\n   - **S&P −10% from its high, about 7,040.** In 2000 the first pullback bottomed at −11%, and ordinary pullbacks rarely go much past this level.\n   - **S&P −20%, about 6,255.** That would be a bear market. In 2000 it took almost a year to get there.\n\nRates are the main risk outside these numbers. The 10-year yield is above 5%, and in 1999–2000 rising yields came before the top.\n\nI added this as section 8 of [`docs/research/dotcom-analog.md`](https://github.com/cv/pinance/blob/main/docs/research/dotcom-analog.md), with both charts and the full lists of matching periods, and pushed it to `main`.\n\n<sub>Method: matches are the closest 4-year (1,008-session) shape matches, from periods at least 250 sessions apart and ending before Nov 2022. Prices are Yahoo Finance daily closes, price only, no dividends. With only 10 matches per index, this is a historical comparison, not a forecast or investment advice.</sub>"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":5370,"cacheRead":174693,"cacheWrite":4379,"totalTokens":184444,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":56},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":17948589